  "body": "Two independent reasons a configured chain sits unused. Both found from the reporter's own request log — 161,812 rows, server on 5.49.0.\n\n---\n\n## 1. A model that only thinks commits the route\n\nThis is the reported failure: `Provider 'nous_portal/tencent/hy3:free' exceeded the 600s request budget`, on a route with **eight models** configured behind it.\n\n```\nbudget failures by model   tencent/hy3:free 479, upstage/solar-pro4:free 9\nroute_attempt on those     0 -> 490,  1 -> 7,  2 -> 2\nthe reported request       ttft 49.4s, thinking 5,518 chars, answer 0 chars, 600.1s\n```\n\nReasoning deltas count as answer content, so **the first thought commits the route**. From then on no other model may take over, the stall guard never fires because thoughts keep arriving, and the request runs until the whole budget ends it. 490 of 499 exhaustions never left attempt 0.\n\n**Nothing the reader has seen is nothing the reader would lose.** With `FALLBACK_ON_REASONING_ONLY` on, reasoning is held in the existing holdback buffer like an envelope frame — the executor sees no chunk, so the attempt keeps its first-token deadline and its share of the budget, expires there, and the next model answers.\n\nThe answer itself still commits exactly as before, and tool arguments are an answer: a tool call is the model acting, not deliberating. `signature_delta` travels with `thinking_delta` — it is the cryptographic tail of a thinking block.\n\n**The cost is real, which is why it is a setting.** Reasoning no longer streams live; it arrives with the answer, or when the buffer's 64 KB cap forces a commit. Default on, because that is what the reporter is hitting. Off restores today's behaviour, on the model config page with the trade stated in the field description.\n\n## 2. A provider in rate-limit cooldown is waited on instead of stepped over\n\nA provider serving a 429 cooldown does not refuse the next request — it accepts it and **sleeps inside its own limiter** until the cooldown expires (up to an hour on `Retry-After`) or the attempt deadline does, then hands the chain a timeout.\n\n`throttle_remaining()` already reported this on every provider; nothing above the provider layer looked. Routing now asks — **only while another candidate remains**, so the last model is tried cooldown or not (Part IV §3: skipping a bad model is an optimisation, refusing to try anything is an outage). A stepped-over model records `skipped` / `cooldown`, not `failed`, and is not counted toward ejection.\n\n`RotatingProvider` inherited `BaseProvider`'s unconditional `0.0`, so a multi-credential provider claimed to be free with every key limited. It now reports the shortest cooldown across its credentials.\n\n**Scope note (§168):** this half was written from the code path *before* the log was consulted, and is **not** credited with the reported failure. Their 429s are rare and last occurred 2026-08-14. It is a real gap on its own.\n\n---\n\n## Also\n\n`FALLBACK_SKIP_KINDS`' help text had never listed `context_length`, added as a kind in 5.43.0.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **9 new tests.** The load-bearing one drives a real provider stream and counts what reached the client while the model was still only thinking — 0 held, >0 not held — with a real 0.8s pause, because without it both settings sit inside the 0.75s holdback window and score identically.\n- **14 mutations, 14 caught.** Including: the provider hop dropped and inverted, the shipped default flipped, `signature_delta` dropped, tool args misclassified as reasoning, the cooldown last-candidate guard dropped, benching a stepped-over model, and `min`→`max`/`min`→`0.0` on the rotating aggregate.\n- One mutation survived first — the early-retry rebuild losing the flag, invisible for exactly the holdback-window reason above. The **test** was strengthened, not the code (§164).\n- Full suite **5013 passed**; the 8 `test_installers.py` failures reproduce identically on unmodified `fork/main` in the same shell.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- Reasoning arriving in a burst rather than live is a visible change for anyone running a reasoning model with the default on. It is one toggle away and the field says so.\n- The cooldown skip can only step over a provider that would have slept, never empties a chain, and is not even queried on single-model routes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
