   "body": "**Correction to the numbers in this PR, and a follow-up fix.**\n\nTwo errors found by auditing this work against the project's own notes after it merged.\n\n**1. The \"479 of 499\" figure is wrong.** 479 is how many of those budget exhaustions ran on one *model* (`tencent/hy3:free`) — not how many had this *mechanism*. I grouped by model and reported it as a mechanism count. The real split of the 499:\n\n```\nnothing at all   401   (the older scaffolding shape, already fixed)\nsome answer       54\nreasoning only    44   <- what this PR addresses\n```\n\nThe reported failure is still a reasoning one, and the mechanism is still real. The prevalence claim was overstated by ~11x. Corrected in the release notes, `.env.example`, the README and the source comments.\n\n**2. The deadline this PR gives a held-reasoning attempt is far too tight.** Holding reasoning makes the attempt look silent to routing, so it inherits the first-token share — `FALLBACK_TOTAL_TIMEOUT` divided by the chain length. On an 11-model chain that is **54 seconds**, which is not enough time for a model to think.\n\nMeasured against the same log:\n\n```\nsuccessful requests that produced reasoning      105,078\n  slower than a 54.5s answer-deadline, with\n  little or no answer (i.e. would be diverted)     1,387\n  same, against a 300s answer-deadline                27\n```\n\nSo as merged this diverts ~1,387 successful requests to rescue ~44 failures. Every one of the 499 exhaustions ran the **full** 600s, so any allowance below that rescues all of them — the tight share buys nothing and costs a lot.\n\nA follow-up adds `FALLBACK_REASONING_ANSWER_TIMEOUT` (default 300s) as a flat allowance, so a thinking attempt is judged by how long it has been thinking rather than by a share sized for a model that has shown nothing.",
