    "message": "feat(routing): a model that only thinks no longer commits the route\n\nReported as \"fallback isn't working\" against\n`Provider 'nous_portal/tencent/hy3:free' exceeded the 600s request budget`\non a route with eight models configured behind it.\n\nThe reporter's request log, 161,812 rows on 5.49.0, names the mechanism:\n\n    budget failures by model   tencent/hy3:free 479, upstage/solar-pro4 9\n    route_attempt on those     0 -> 490,  1 -> 7,  2 -> 2\n    the reported request       ttft 49.4s, thinking 5,518 chars,\n                               answer 0 chars, 600.1s\n\nReasoning deltas count as answer content, so the first thought commits the\nroute. From that moment no other model may take over, the stall guard never\nfires because thoughts keep arriving, and the request runs until the whole\nbudget ends it. A model that thinks for ten minutes and never writes a word\ntherefore spends an eight-model chain on nothing -- 490 of 499 exhaustions\nnever left attempt 0.\n\nNothing the reader has seen is nothing the reader would lose. With\nFALLBACK_ON_REASONING_ONLY on, reasoning is held in the existing holdback\nbuffer like an envelope frame: the executor sees no chunk, so the attempt\nkeeps its first-token deadline and its share of the budget, expires there,\nand the next model answers. The answer itself still commits exactly as\nbefore, and tool arguments are an answer -- a tool call is the model acting,\nnot deliberating.\n\n`signature_delta` travels with `thinking_delta`: it is the cryptographic\ntail of a thinking block and means nothing without it.\n\nThe cost is real and is the reason this is a setting rather than a change:\nreasoning no longer streams live, arriving with the answer or when the\nbuffer's 64 KB cap forces a commit. Default on, because the measurement\nabove is what the reporter is running into; off restores the old behaviour\nand is on the model config page with that trade stated.\n\nAlso fixed in passing: the FALLBACK_SKIP_KINDS help text had never listed\n`context_length`, added as a kind in 5.43.0.\n\nVerification: 9 tests. The load-bearing one drives a real provider stream\nand counts what reached the client while the model was still only thinking\n-- 0 held, >0 not held -- with a real 0.8s pause, because without it both\nsettings sit inside the 0.75s holdback window and score the same. Eight\nmutations, all caught, including the provider hop dropped and inverted and\nthe shipped default flipped. One survived first: the early-retry rebuild\nlosing the flag was invisible for exactly the window reason above, so the\ntest was strengthened rather than the code. Full suite 5013 passed with the\n8 pre-existing PowerShell installer failures unchanged from fork/main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
